{"id":"n5-116","title":"なにか～","romaji":"nanika～","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Indicates 'something' or 'some kind of'.","longExplanation":"The なにか grammar point is used to express the idea of 'something' or 'some kind of' in Japanese. It is often used when the speaker is unsure or not specific about the details of the noun being referred to. なにか is used before the noun it modifies.","formation":"なにか + Noun","examples":[{"jp":"なにか飲み物を持ってきてください。","romaji":"Nanika nomimono wo motte kite kudasai.","en":"Please bring some kind of drink.","words":[{"surface":"なにか","vocabId":"1188270","reading":"なにか"},{"surface":"飲み物","vocabId":"1600430","reading":"のみもの"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"持っ","vocabId":"1315720","reading":"もつ","baseForm":"持つ"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"き","vocabId":"1221520","reading":"き","baseForm":"くる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"なにか質問があれば、遠慮なく聞いてください。","romaji":"Nanika shitsumon ga areba, enryo naku kiite kudasai.","en":"If you have any questions, please feel free to ask.","words":[{"surface":"なに","vocabId":"1577100","reading":"なに"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"質問","vocabId":"1320760","reading":"しつもん"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"あれ","vocabId":"1857320","reading":"あれ","baseForm":"ある"},{"surface":"ば","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"遠慮なく","vocabId":"1178460","reading":"えんりょなく","baseForm":"遠慮ない"},{"surface":"聞い","vocabId":"1591110","reading":"きく","baseForm":"聞く"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0,1]},{"jp":"彼女はなにかプレゼントを持っている。","romaji":"Kanojo wa nanika purezento wo motte iru.","en":"She has some kind of present.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null}